    "title": "Cameron Young, former Westchester resident, wins Players Championship",
    "text": "Cameron Young, former Westchester resident, wins Players ChampionshipCameron Young won The Players Championship.Young missed a birdie putt from just off the back but left his par putt just inches away. Then, from 8 feet, 9 inches, Matt Fitzpatrick missed his par putt and Young tapped in for the win on March 15 at TPC Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, Florida.AdvertisementYoung, 28, grew up in Garrison and formerly resided in Scarborough. His father David was the longtime head professional at Sleepy Hollow Country Club. He attended Fordham Prep and often spent winters in Florida working on his game.Young, who now lives in Jupiter, Florida, played collegiately at Wake Forest.1 / 15Mar 15, 2026; Ponte Vedra Beach, Florida, USA; Cameron Young watches his tee shot on the first hole during the final round of THE PLAYERS Championship golf tournament. Mandatory Credit: Jeff Romance-Imagn Images2 / 15Cameron Thomas, former Westchester resident, wins Players ChampionshipMar 15, 2026; Ponte Vedra Beach, Florida, USA; Cameron Young plays his approach shot to the second hole during the final round of THE PLAYERS Championship golf tournament. Mandatory Credit: Jeff Romance-Imagn Images15 / 15Cameron Thomas, former Westchester resident, wins Players ChampionshipCameron Young makes his way down the 5th fairway during the final round ofThe Players Championship at The Players Stadium Course at TPC Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, Fla. Sunday March 15, 2026. [Doug Engle/Florida Times-Union]Young finished the tournament 13-under-par.In 2025, Young was on the U.S. Ryder Cup team at Bethpage Black.Players Championship leaderboardThe 2026 Players Championship leaderboard is complete. Here's the top of the board after 72 holes:Pos.PlayerTotalThru1Cameron Young-13F2Matt Fitzpatrick-12F3Xander Schauffele-11F4Robert MacIntyre-10FContributing: GolfWeekThis article originally appeared on Rockland/Westchester Journal News: Cameron Young, former Westchester resident, wins Players Championship",
